---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import BlochShield from '../components/BlochShield.svelte';
---

<Shell
  title="Privacy — QuantumShield"
  description="QuantumShield privacy posture for the local CLI and optional browser workflow."
>
  <div style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);">
    <div style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:14px 24px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;">
      <a href="/" class="brand hstack" style="font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);">
        <BlochShield size={24} />
        <span>QuantumShield</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/security" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);">Security</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 32px 80px;">
    <div class="tiny-caps" style="color:var(--navy-600);">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="serif" style="font-size:34px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.015em;margin:6px 0 10px;">
      Your org data stays in your execution environment.
    </h1>
    <p style="font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-3);line-height:1.65;max-width:700px;">
      QuantumShield is designed as a read-only scanner with no QuantumShield data
      proxy. CLI scans run on your machine. Browser scans run in your tab and talk
      directly to your Salesforce instance.
    </p>

    <section style="display:grid;gap:16px;margin-top:32px;">
      <article class="qs-card qs-card-body">
        <h2 class="serif" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 8px;">What QuantumShield stores</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;">
          The CLI writes reports only to the output directory you choose. Browser
          mode stores scan history and reports in IndexedDB on this device. Browser
          OAuth session material is kept in session storage and is discarded when
          the tab session ends. The browser may remember your Salesforce client ID
          and region preference in local storage.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="qs-card qs-card-body">
        <h2 class="serif" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 8px;">What QuantumShield does not collect</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;">
          QuantumShield does not collect Salesforce record data, field values,
          attachments, files, org scan results, OAuth tokens, or generated reports.
          Static hosting logs may record ordinary web requests for pages and assets.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="qs-card qs-card-body">
        <h2 class="serif" style="font-size:22px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 8px;">Control and deletion</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;">
          CLI artifacts are ordinary local files. Browser-mode scan history can be
          cleared from the app overview. Revoking the customer-owned External Client
          App or Connected App in Salesforce ends future browser access for that
          client ID.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</Shell>
